Folded sheet of eleven visiting cards and a letter, all belonging to the Banks family; dated by Banks between 1779-1792; [] indicates hand written notes:
<p><br>
<br>C,1.716: Mr Banks / Gray fecit;
<br>C,1.717-718: Mr Banks / New Burlington Street;
<br>C,1.719, 721: Mr Banks / Soho Square;
<br>C,1.720: Mr Banks presents his Compliments / to / &amp; requests the Honor of / Company / at Dinner on / Soho Square / The favor of an answer is requested;
<br>C,1.722: Sir Joseph  &amp; Lady Banks present their Compts to and request the Honor of Company at Dinner on / Soho Square / Dinner at / the favor of an Answer is requested; [1781]
<br>C,1.723: Mrs Banks Soho Square; [1779]
<br>C,1.724: Lady Banks Soho Square; [1781]
<br>C,1.725: Lady Banks; [Jany 1787]
</p>
<br>C,1.726: manuscript letter dated April 16 1792, signed by Joseph Banks, inviting the recipient to a Committee meeting proposing to re-route a river;
